---
import ProjectPage from '../components/ProjectPage.astro';
---

<ProjectPage
	title="Anuva Cleaning"
	subtitle="Cincinnati commercial cleaning. Built to perform."
	image="anuvaCleaning.png"
	alt="Home page of Anuva, a Cincinnati commercial cleaning company, over a photo of the Cincinnati skyline"
	url="https://anuvacleaning.com"
	cta="Visit the live site"
	tags={['Website', 'Live site']}
>
	<p>
		The website for Anuva, a woman- and minority-owned commercial cleaning and facility services company that has
		served greater Cincinnati since 2014. It speaks to government, construction, healthcare, education and large-venue
		clients, and turns visits into quote requests.
	</p>

	<Fragment slot="details">
		<div>
			<h2>What the site does</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Leads with the offer:</strong> a skyline hero with the headline, a one-line pitch and two actions, Request a quote and View our services.</li>
				<li><strong>Builds trust fast:</strong> a strip of credentials (woman and minority-owned, government contract experience, prevailing-wage capable, fully insured, established 2014) and a panel of certifications.</li>
				<li><strong>Sorts visitors by industry:</strong> government, construction, commercial, healthcare, education, and large venues and events, each with its own short pitch.</li>
				<li><strong>Lists the services:</strong> commercial janitorial, construction cleaning, day porter services, floor care, event and venue cleaning, and disinfecting.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<div>
			<h2>Built for public contracts</h2>
			<p>
				A dedicated government contracting section explains that wage determinations and certified payroll are reviewed
				before every project, which matters to the public-sector buyers the company bids for.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div>
			<h2>Proof of work</h2>
			<p>
				A recent-projects section shows real engagements by sector: six months of hospital cleaning at UC Hospital, two
				years of ongoing service for StandardAero, event and ongoing cleaning for the Cincinnati Open tennis
				tournament, and day porter services across seven Sharonville schools.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div>
			<h2>Pages</h2>
			<p>Home, Services, Industries, Government contracting, About, and a Request a quote form.</p>
		</div>
	</Fragment>
</ProjectPage>
